      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty intense way to put it. You mentioned they're \"aimed at dismantling decades of progress\"—can you walk me through the specific legal merits of the opposition's case? For instance, when they cite the 14th Amendment or the concept of \"colorblindness\" in the Constitution, are those considered legitimate interpretations of current law by most scholars, or is that also just part of the \"strategic\" rebranding you're talking about?",
