      "content": "I see. You're saying that the \"colorblind\" interpretation is essentially a misreading of the law. But if we look at how the Supreme Court has trended recently, especially with the SFFA v. Harvard decision, it seems like the legal consensus is shifting quite significantly. \n\nIf the Court is effectively deciding that race-conscious admissions are no longer permissible under the Equal Protection Clause, isn't it a bit reductive to call that a \"misinterpretation\"? Even if it deviates from Grutter, doesn't that mean there's a genuine, high-level debate about what the Constitution actually requires today, rather than just one side being \"wrong\" about its meaning?",
